{"agent_id":"pp3g-TExl-planning-task-zero-context-plan-only-no-92da","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T20:15:28.439735678Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4fd047c3-b6ed-46a2-9b26-0f90cc14c782","comment_uuid":"24bbb342-7ca7-4244-9b0d-5030d4722aca","author":"pp3g-TExl-planning-task-zero-context-plan-only-no-92da","content":"Plan: zero-context remediation plan for B1-B6. Evidence gathering complete (read-only): (1) rules ownership matrix computed across fork/Tools/ASES/tripn — 28/31 binary rules byte-identical, global.md/knowledge.md/project.md/kickoff.md are layer-owned overrides (ASES global.md has Background-processes rule Tools lacks; kickoff.md ASES-only); (2) tripn-astro has NO .ases/ dir (recursive find = 0), but EDASES-Methodology-Feedback-and-Enforcement.md EXISTS in ASES/docs/research/ describing .ases/ as aspirational design (§3); tripn IS crosslink-tracked with .opencode/plugins + .crosslink/rules + hook-config.json — concrete sync targets exist; (3) no consumer-side check exists anywhere: ASES+tripn opencode.json both load ./plugins/*.ts locally, Tools has no opencode.json; #274 pattern = consumer fail-loud guard verified in live opencode wrapper; (4) Tools/.claude/settings.json wires 6 live hooks; on-disk Tools+ASES work-check.py use OLD returncode==2 logic; fork resources + installed binary (37789b51) use NEW returncode!=2 fail-open JSON-flags protocol — rm+re-init = behavior change; (5) Tools git: branch main, ahead 1, uncommitted scripts/claude+global.md, untracked .opencode/+.worktrees/; no cutover machinery; (6) live claude has --agent/CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE/--auto/correct-quoting + memory-scope; Tools copy lacks --agent, has PROMPT quoting bug, wrong provider list; live opencode has #274 fork guard + .exe REAL path, Tools lacks both; crosslink-moe identical. Deliverable: per-blocker resolution (a) recommendation+rationale (b) alternatives (c) plan-delta (d) cheapest discriminating test, plus revised 6-step ordering + risk register, posted as --kind result.","created_at":"2026-08-14T20:15:28.430201302Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:NTm9QsLsdb/zOTM8xXtaWMU7wteL3FirFVWnTgSAAk0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgttxanJFV/dDT4qsuEY7JxGarkERZbF0WJblKg1FrdYwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAQm8xBz9qucRBTSqaDCzWc39xX3EZnxA8qkthUFeMTW1KBLnpc+oijVGD4dNLltFWqhVS1AaP5SuUyDcJViMwAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:NTm9QsLsdb/zOTM8xXtaWMU7wteL3FirFVWnTgSAAk0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgttxanJFV/dDT4qsuEY7JxGarkERZbF0WJblKg1FrdYwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK31gV9YvinvWP+ys0Tq3leYWTIxzz7Rro7ApKxGUlDWeSxXsDcfNGgN44C1Z45AdYHUtKyeeaCsF0/DorFIqQI="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-TExl-planning-task-zero-context-plan-only-no-92da","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T20:15:50.197169932Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4fd047c3-b6ed-46a2-9b26-0f90cc14c782","comment_uuid":"8f913bf8-1f35-4ed5-96bc-69c8ef066dd4","author":"pp3g-TExl-planning-task-zero-context-plan-only-no-92da","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=plan posted; all six blockers verified on disk (rules ownership matrix, tripn boundary absence, enforcement-point gap, hook behavior delta, cutover gaps, wrapper contract deltas) next=compose per-blocker resolution + revised plan + risk register blocker=none","created_at":"2026-08-14T20:15:50.190836901Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:NTm9QsLsdb/zOTM8xXtaWMU7wteL3FirFVWnTgSAAk0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgttxanJFV/dDT4qsuEY7JxGarkERZbF0WJblKg1FrdYwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAC1HxGAXf6mokBLtfOUMj+7W3PHItIuNilhUSzcHUUmH7KMyTur2CXLhNkMtOUm8UqmGsUfuLpSOO84E7lQhsDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:NTm9QsLsdb/zOTM8xXtaWMU7wteL3FirFVWnTgSAAk0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgttxanJFV/dDT4qsuEY7JxGarkERZbF0WJblKg1FrdYwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIgcyVnWf9LMLwZB05urjv8hYyICVULLbomcqNoIt/tF7vWs4wwnGYNktWO9donMDrQzO6DOVBhgDwvMKvT6kAg="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-TExl-planning-task-zero-context-plan-only-no-92da","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T20:17:38.005772267Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4fd047c3-b6ed-46a2-9b26-0f90cc14c782","comment_uuid":"32df84f9-3988-426e-918f-85b1ac430756","author":"pp3g-TExl-planning-task-zero-context-plan-only-no-92da","content":"# REMEDIATION PLAN — Tools monorepo migration blockers B1–B6 (#361)\n\nZERO-CONTEXT planning task. Read-only: no files changed, no commits. Evidence verified on disk 2026-08-14 from ASES (this worktree), Tools, tripn-astro, crosslink fork, and ~/.local/bin. All six findings confirmed present and accurate; resolutions below are grounded in the actual file state.\n\nEVIDENCE SNAPSHOT (used throughout):\n- Rules matrix (md5 across fork-resources / Tools / ASES / tripn): 28 of 31 binary rules byte-identical everywhere; `global.md` differs in ALL FOUR places (fork 9893B, Tools 10188B, ASES 10442B, tripn 10454B); `knowledge.md` fork=Tools(1756B)≠ASES(2906B); `project.md` fork=Tools(274B)≠ASES(1161B)≠tripn; `kickoff.md` ASES-only (4810B); `tooling.md` Tools=ASES(882B), absent from fork.\n- `ASES/.crosslink/rules/global.md:117` has the \"Background processes\" (nohup) rule; Tools' copy lacks it; tripn has it at :118. ASES adds `kickoff.md` (absent from Tools + fork).\n- tripn-astro: NO `.ases/` dir (recursive find = 0). `EDASES-methodology-enforcement.md` absent everywhere, but its successor doc EXISTS at `ASES/docs/research/EDASES-Methodology-Feedback-and-Enforcement.md` (§3 documents `.ases/` as an ASPIRATIONAL integration-boundary design — `.ases/manifest.yaml`, `.ases/events/` — not an implemented mechanism). tripn IS crosslink-tracked: `.opencode/opencode.json` loads `./plugins/*.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/` has all 3 guard plugins, `.crosslink/rules/` has 30 files, `.crosslink/hook-config.json` exists.\n- Consumer loading: ASES and tripn both load guard plugins from their OWN `.opencode/plugins/`. Tools has NO `.opencode/opencode.json` (only command/, node_modules/, package.json — untracked) — Tools is warehouse-only, nothing consumes Tools/plugins today.\n- Hooks: `Tools/.claude/settings.json` wires 6 live hooks (post-edit-check, heartbeat, pre-web-check, work-check, session-start, prompt-guard). On-disk Tools+ASES `work-check.py` = OLD logic (`if proc.returncode == 0: return; if proc.returncode == 2: parse`, calls `[\"crosslink\",\"agent\",\"flags\"]`). Fork resources = NEW logic (`if proc.returncode != 2: return` then JSON-parse, uses `find_crosslink_binary`). Installed binary = `0.9.0-beta.1+37789b51-dirty` == fork HEAD `37789b51`.\n- Wrappers: live `~/.local/bin/claude` (3039B) has `--agent`, `CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE`, tmux `--auto`, memory-scope systemd-run, correct `\"$PROMPT\"` quoting, provider list incl. `opencode`. Tools/scripts/claude (2443B + uncommitted) lacks `--agent`, passes `--dangerously-skip-permissions` through, has `${PROMPT:+\\\"\\\"}` quoting bug, provider list missing `opencode`. Live `~/.local/bin/opencode` (3639B) has the #274 fork-identity guard (FORK_MARKER scan ≥ 2, fail-closed exit 1, version fallback) and REAL→`.../opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe`; Tools copy (1498B) has no guard and REAL→`.../bin/opencode`. `crosslink-moe`: IDENTICAL.\n- Plugins: ASES crosslink-guard.ts 42140B (75 \"agent\" refs, 0 hardcoded project paths), tripn 37584B (42 refs), Tools 33476B. ASES is a functional superset + repo-agnostic.\n- Tools git: branch `main`, ahead of origin by 1, uncommitted `scripts/claude` (+13-3) and `.crosslink/rules/global.md` (+1), untracked `.claude/findings-interrupt-plugin.md`, `.opencode/`, `.worktrees/`.\n- Non-blocking: TOOLING.md §1.1/§1.2 claim \"(identical copies)\" — false. §16 describes the crosslink repo but never calls it a fork or states embedded-resource authority. hook-config.json: ASES `comment_discipline=encouraged`/`signing_enforcement=audit` + by_type.builder; tripn `required`/`enforced` + orchestrator gates `git worktree remove`. No EDASES/Execution dirs on disk.\n\n---\n\n## B1 — D3↔D4 contradiction on rules → sync would clobber layer overrides\n\n### (a) Recommended resolution\n**Exclude `.crosslink/rules` from sync-tooling.sh entirely; document a three-class per-path ownership map instead of syncing.**\n\nThe md5 matrix proves the rules split cleanly:\n1. **Binary-distributed (28 files)** — language rules + tracking modes + quality/rigor/sanitize-patterns. Already byte-identical across fork/Tools/ASES/tripn because `crosslink init` deploys them from the binary. They need NO sync — the binary is the source, exactly as D3's \"mirror-not-synced\" says. Any sync copy of these is a redundant write that can only drift.\n2. **Layer-owned (4 files)** — `global.md`, `knowledge.md`, `project.md`, `kickoff.md`. Each layer overrides them deliberately: ASES global.md adds \"Background processes\" (nohup) + full Documentation-Trail/Intervention-Logging sections; tripn global.md adds its own overrides; ASES adds `kickoff.md` wholesale. Syncing Tools→layer would destroy these overrides — this is exactly the clobber the reviewers flagged. These stay layer-owned, never synced, per-path documented.\n3. **Tools-owned (1 file)** — `tooling.md` (the catalog pointer). It is already identical in Tools and ASES and is not in the fork. This is the only rules-path file a sync script could legitimately carry — and even this is optional, since both copies already match and the knowledge page is the real pointer.\n\n`sync-tooling.sh` therefore copies **plugins + wrappers + the 2 crosslink skills** only; `rules/` is excluded from the copy manifest by default, with a `--include-rules` explicit opt-in flag that warns loudly. The ownership map lives in TOOLING.md §(source-of-truth map) and is machine-readable (the script's manifest).\n\nRationale: preserves layer overrides (the reviewers' core concern), matches the verified file reality (binary already distributes the identical subset), and keeps the sync surface minimal — fewer copy paths = fewer drift surfaces.\n\n### (b) Alternatives considered\n- **Per-path ownership map + sync only the binary-distributed subset**: rejected because the binary subset is already identical everywhere — copying it adds writes with zero benefit and a nonzero chance of introducing divergence (e.g., if a layer's rules were temporarily edited).\n- **Sync everything except the 4 layer-owned files**: functionally equivalent to exclusion for rules, but keeps a confusing \"syncs rules except...\" contract; exclusion is simpler and matches D3's mirror-not-synced wording.\n- **Create the map but still sync tooling.md only**: acceptable fallback; the plan carries tooling.md as Tools-owned either way (already in sync today).\n\n### (c) What it changes in the 6-step plan\n- Step 3 (sync-tooling.sh): manifest excludes `.crosslink/rules` (default); copies plugins/wrappers/skills only.\n- Step 4 (TOOLING.md): source-of-truth map lists the three-class rules ownership (binary-distributed / layer-owned / Tools-owned) with the per-file matrix as a table.\n\n### (d) Cheapest discriminating test\nRun the existing md5 comparison (28/31 identical; 4 divergent as documented) as a script check before building anything: if any of the 28 \"binary-distributed\" files differs from the fork resources, the binary was rebuilt/init not re-run and the premise fails — stop and re-init instead of building a sync script on a wrong baseline. Cost: one md5 loop, minutes.\n\n---\n\n## B2 — D4's tripn `.ases/` boundary does not exist\n\n### (a) Recommended resolution\n**Drop the `.ases/` boundary from the sync design; sync directly to tripn's real crosslink-tracked paths: `tripn/.opencode/plugins` + `tripn/.crosslink/rules` (rules excluded per B1), + document the boundary as aspirational.**\n\nVerified: tripn is already a fully crosslink-tracked repo — it has `.opencode/opencode.json` referencing `./plugins/*.ts`, all 3 guard plugins in `.opencode/plugins/`, 30 files in `.crosslink/rules/`, and its own `.crosslink/hook-config.json`. The concrete sync targets exist TODAY. The `.ases/` concept is real but aspirational: its successor doc `ASES/docs/research/EDASES-Methodology-Feedback-and-Enforcement.md` §3 defines `.ases/manifest.yaml` + `.ases/events/` as a **proposed** project integration boundary — nothing implements it, and tripn has no `.ases/` directory. Building step 3 on a nonexistent path was the review's point; the fix is to target what exists.\n\nSync destination for the tripn leg: `tripn/.opencode/plugins/{crosslink-guard,orchestrator-guard,rtk-guard}.ts`. (Rules: excluded per B1 — tripn's `global.md` is layer-owned and already has its own overrides.) TOOLING.md + the knowledge page get a one-line note: \".ases/ boundary per EDASES-Methodology-Feedback-and-Enforcement.md §3 is design-stage; sync targets the live crosslink dirs.\"\n\nRationale: zero new infrastructure, uses the path tripn actually loads from, keeps the door open for `.ases/` when/if methodology enforces it, and removes the false dependency from the script.\n\n### (b) Alternatives considered\n- **Create+document `.ases/` first, then sync through it**: rejected for this migration — it builds new methodology infrastructure (manifest/events, per the design doc) that is explicitly out of scope for a Tools-migration remediation, and the design doc does not define a copy-path mechanism, only an event boundary.\n- **Drop the tripn leg from scope entirely**: rejected as the primary resolution because tripn consumes the guard plugins today; without a tripn leg the 3-way plugin divergence (already 36.7K vs 41.2K) will simply persist client-side. Kept as a documented fallback if the operator prefers to defer client wiring to a later pass.\n\n### (c) What it changes in the 6-step plan\n- Step 3 (sync-tooling.sh): tripn leg writes to `tripn/.opencode/plugins` directly; `.ases/` mentioned only in docs, never in code paths.\n- Step 4 (TOOLING.md): the source-of-truth map's tripn row says \"sync target = tripn/.opencode/plugins; .ases/ = aspirational design (EDASES-Methodology-Feedback-and-Enforcement.md §3)\".\n\n### (d) Cheapest discriminating test\nBefore wiring the tripn leg, run `ls tripn/.opencode/plugins/` and `ls tripn/.crosslink/rules/` and confirm tripn's `opencode.json` plugin array — already done, all present. Then a dry-run of the tripn leg against a `--dry-run` flag must report exactly 3 file writes and no rules writes. Cost: minutes.\n\n---\n\n## B3 — No consumer-side enforcement point for the canonical-source claim\n\n### (a) Recommended resolution\n**Add a consumption-time drift check to the guard-plugin startup path, mirroring the #274 fail-loud pattern, plus a `sync-tooling.sh --check` preflight command.**\n\nThe #274 pattern (live opencode wrapper) works because the check runs on the consumer side, on every invocation, and FAILS LOUDLY. D4's checksum marker has no consumer. Design:\n1. **Marker file**: sync-tooling.sh writes a small manifest at each destination — `Tools/plugins/.canonical-manifest.json` containing per-file sha256 + a source commit/tag + timestamp. Consumers do not depend on Tools being present at runtime.\n2. **Consumer-side check (guard plugin startup)**: extend `crosslink-guard.ts` (the plugin every repo already loads at every session) so that on session start it compares its own loaded file's checksum against the recorded canonical checksum embedded in the marker. Two modes:\n   - `fail-loud` (default after sync is proven): if mismatch → refuse to enforce guard guarantees and print a prominent \"DRIFT: plugins out of sync with Tools canonical — run sync-tooling.sh\" banner to the session log (mirrors #274's fail-closed refusal).\n   - `warn` (transition mode, initially): log the mismatch to `/tmp/crosslink-guard.log` + banner, keep enforcing. This avoids wedging sessions during the migration window.\n3. **Preflight command**: `sync-tooling.sh --check` compares every destination file's checksum against the canonical manifest and exits non-zero listing every drifted path — the explicit \"who runs it, when, what fails loudly\": run it in the agent preflight rule or the operator's release checklist.\n\nAlso fixes the D1 workflow inversion explicitly: the consumer-side check is what makes \"canonical is Tools\" stick — a developer editing ASES/.opencode/plugins directly will see the drift banner/refusal on next session, so the natural dev loop becomes edit-Tools → sync → verify, instead of edit-ASES → Tools silently stale.\n\nRationale: closes the exact gap the reviewers identified (no consumer, no fail-loud trigger, D1 inversion); reuses the #274 pattern the plan already cites; the transition warn-mode de-risks rollout.\n\n### (b) Alternatives considered\n- **Guard-plugin startup marker check only, hard-fail immediately**: rejected as the initial mode — if the sync is not yet proven, a hard fail could wedge every consumer repo at once; use warn-mode first, hard-fail after the sync has been exercised.\n- **Preflight-only (no startup check)**: rejected as the sole mechanism — preflight runs on demand and misses the \"session start\" moment where drift first manifests.\n- **Rule-injection check (a preflight rule)**: viable complement; listed as optional in step 6, not the primary point because the guard plugin is already loaded everywhere and needs no new injection path.\n\n### (c) What it changes in the 6-step plan\n- Step 3: sync-tooling.sh additionally writes `.canonical-manifest.json` at destinations and gains `--check`.\n- Step 6: consumer wiring now includes the marker check in crosslink-guard.ts (warn-mode first, hard-fail after proven) + preflight rule hook-in.\n\n### (d) Cheapest discriminating test\nBefore touching crosslink-guard.ts: write a 5-line shell check that hashes one file, tampers a copy, and exits non-zero on mismatch — proving the checksum mechanism itself works. Then test the plugin change by loading a deliberately stale plugin copy in a scratch repo and confirming the banner appears (warn mode) and, after flipping to hard-fail, that enforcement is refused. Cost: minutes for the hash test; one session for the plugin-load test.\n\n---\n\n## B4 — Step 5 (rm gitignored hooks/commands/mcp) has no re-deploy step and changes runtime behavior\n\n### (a) Recommended resolution\n**Re-sequence step 5: pin the crosslink binary version FIRST, then run the exact sequence rm → `crosslink init` → verify, with the behavior change documented and accepted; do NOT run rm bare.**\n\nVerified on disk: `Tools/.claude/settings.json` wires 6 live hooks; on-disk Tools hooks match the OLD embedded version (`work-check.py`: `if proc.returncode == 0: return; if proc.returncode == 2: parse`), while the installed binary (`0.9.0-beta.1+37789b51-dirty` == fork HEAD `37789b51`) and fork resources carry the NEW version (`if proc.returncode != 2: return` + JSON flags parse + `find_crosslink_binary`). So:\n- bare `rm` → Tools agents run with NO hooks (settings.json resolves `.claude/hooks/*.py`; the `if [ -f ]` guards mean silent no-op → work-check/prompt-guard/heartbeat/session-start all die);\n- `rm` + re-init from the current binary → hook behavior CHANGES (returncode semantics: new logic fail-opens on anything-but-2+valid-JSON and resolves the crosslink binary via `find_crosslink_binary`, not PATH).\n\nExact sequence (step 5):\n1. Record the pinned binary identity (version + fork commit + build date) in TOOLING.md §16, and note \"on-disk hooks in any repo are stale until `crosslink init` re-run from this binary\".\n2. Document the behavior delta in TOOLING.md (old: exit-0 pass / exit-2 flags; new: exit-2 + valid JSON = flags, else fail-open; crosslink binary resolution change).\n3. `rm -rf Tools/.claude/hooks Tools/.claude/commands Tools/.claude/mcp` (gitignored — nothing tracked is lost).\n4. `crosslink init` in Tools from the pinned binary.\n5. Verify: hooks exist again, settings.json still resolves each of the 6 hooks, `work-check.py` contains the NEW `!= 2` logic, and a smoke test (e.g., run the agent flags path) returns the new semantics.\n6. Do the same for ASES (its on-disk hooks are equally stale) — as part of the same sequenced cutover, not a separate surprise.\n\nIf the operator prefers zero runtime-behavior change during the migration window, the alternative is to **defer step 5 entirely** (keep the stale on-disk hooks; they work, they are just old) until the fork binary is rebuilt and the behavior change is an explicit, separate change. Both are acceptable; the recommended path pins the binary + documents the delta, because the on-disk snapshots are a known confusion source.\n\nRationale: the reviewers are right that step 5 as written is a live-wiring footgun; the fix is not \"don't remove\" but \"remove inside a pinned, verified sequence that makes the behavior change explicit\".\n\n### (b) Alternatives considered\n- **Defer step 5 until binary rebuild**: viable; documented as fallback. Keeps current behavior, leaves stale snapshots in place longer.\n- **rm + re-init + verify only in Tools, skip ASES**: rejected — ASES hooks are equally stale (verified: ASES work-check.py has the same old `returncode == 2` logic), and an asymmetric hook version between the two repos that both agents use is worse than either uniform state.\n\n### (c) What it changes in the 6-step plan\n- Step 5 becomes a 6-part pinned sequence (record → document delta → rm → init → verify → ASES mirror) and is re-sequenced AFTER step 3 (so the sync tool exists before hook deployment changes).\n- Step 4's TOOLING.md update includes the binary pin + behavior delta.\n\n### (d) Cheapest discriminating test\nOn a scratch worktree (e.g., a throwaway `crosslink init` target): run the rm → init → verify sequence and confirm (i) hooks are re-deployed from the pinned binary, (ii) settings.json hooks resolve, (iii) `work-check.py` shows the `!= 2` logic. If the scratch run leaves hooks in a broken state, abort step 5 in Tools. Cost: ~10 minutes.\n\n---\n\n## B5 — No cutover transaction for cross-repo writes\n\n### (a) Recommended resolution\n**Give sync-tooling.sh a transactional cutover protocol: clean-worktree precondition, local-edit preservation, atomic staging, dry-run, partial-failure detection, rollback, per-repo verification.**\n\nRequired preconditions and behaviors, each verified against Tools' actual state:\n1. **Clean-worktree precondition (per repo)**: `git status --porcelain` must be empty in Tools and every destination before any cross-repo write. Tools currently FAILS this: uncommitted `scripts/claude`, `.crosslink/rules/global.md`, untracked `.opencode/`, `.worktrees/`. So step 0 of the revised plan is: commit or stash Tools' uncommitted changes FIRST (the `scripts/claude` uncommitted delta is the memory-scope change that must be merged into the canonical wrapper per D2 anyway — it becomes part of the canonical commit, not a loose change).\n2. **Local-edit preservation**: the script must refuse to overwrite a destination file whose checksum differs from BOTH the canonical source AND the last-synced manifest entry (i.e., a local edit exists) — report and skip, never silently clobber.\n3. **Dry-run**: `sync-tooling.sh --dry-run` prints the exact per-repo file ops (path, action, checksum before/after) and exits without writing. Mandatory before every real run.\n4. **Atomic staging**: write each destination file to `*.sync-tmp` then rename into place; on any failure, delete temp files; record a per-run transaction log (`Tools/.sync-state/<timestamp>.json`) listing each op as pending/done.\n5. **Partial-failure detection**: exit non-zero on the first failed op; the transaction log marks completed ops so a re-run can resume without double-copying.\n6. **Rollback**: before each overwrite, back up the existing destination file to `Tools/.sync-backup/<timestamp>/<repo>/<path>`; a `--rollback <timestamp>` flag restores all files from a given run.\n7. **Per-repo verification**: after a real run, for each destination repo, `git status --porcelain` must show exactly the synced files and nothing else; then run `sync-tooling.sh --check` (B3) and, for plugin consumers, the guard startup check.\n\nRationale: matches the reviewer's requirement list exactly and grounds it in the verified Tools state — the first cutover action is cleaning Tools' own worktree, which is also a D2 merge prerequisite.\n\n### (b) Alternatives considered\n- **Manual per-repo copy with operator review**: rejected — the whole point is drift detection and reproducibility; manual copies reintroduce the 3-way divergence failure mode.\n- **Reversible commits only (no backup dir)**: rejected as the sole mechanism — commits are the right per-repo record but a `.sync-backup` directory gives byte-level rollback without git history surgery in consumer repos.\n\n### (c) What it changes in the 6-step plan\n- Adds step 0: clean Tools worktree (commit the uncommitted wrapper + global.md deltas as the canonicalization baseline).\n- Step 3 gains the full transaction protocol above.\n- Step 6's verification uses the B3 `--check` + guard startup check as the acceptance gate.\n\n### (d) Cheapest discriminating test\n`sync-tooling.sh --dry-run` against ASES (the only existing consumer) must print exactly the intended file ops with zero writes (verify via `git status` unchanged); then a deliberately-tampered destination file must trigger the local-edit refusal path. Cost: minutes.\n\n---\n\n## B6 — D1/D2 lack provenance + cheapest discriminating tests\n\n### (a) Recommended resolution\n**Capture exact provenance for every canonicalized file, then run a wrapper-contract test battery BEFORE writing the canonical copies.**\n\nProvenance to record (all verified on disk today):\n- `Tools/scripts/claude` canonical = LIVE `~/.local/bin/claude` (3039B, Aug 1) — the review's \"merge premise is stale\" is correct: the live copy ALREADY contains memory-scope + `--agent` + `CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE` + tmux `--auto` + correct quoting. Tools' copy (2443B + uncommitted) is strictly behind except it has the memory-scope delta as an uncommitted change — which the live copy already has. **Step 1 is effectively: replace Tools copy with the live copy**, then drop the uncommitted delta (already contained), then the two match. Post-merge functional check required.\n- `Tools/scripts/opencode` canonical = LIVE `~/.local/bin/opencode` (3639B, Aug 9) with the #274 fork-identity guard and REAL→`.../opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe`. Tools' copy (1498B) is strictly behind (no guard, different REAL).\n- `Tools/scripts/crosslink-moe` = already identical to live (verified byte-for-byte).\n- `Tools/plugins/*` canonical = ASES `.opencode/plugins/*` (crosslink-guard 42140B, orchestrator-guard 3816B, rtk-guard 13893B). Authority evidence: functional superset (75 vs 42 \"agent\" refs) + repo-agnostic (0 hardcoded project paths) — record THIS, not size, per the review.\n- Deploy path back to `~/.local/bin`: after Tools is canonical, sync-tooling.sh's wrapper leg must deploy Tools/scripts → `~/.local/bin` (or the plan must state `~/.local/bin` is the deploy target of the wrapper leg). The current plan has no deploy path back; TOOLING.md §1.1/§1.2 falsely claim \"(identical copies)\". Fix both.\n\nWrapper contract test battery (cheapest discriminating tests, run in a scratch dir before writing canonical files):\n1. `--agent` mapping: `claude --agent builder --model opencode-go/X \"p\"` must pass `--agent builder` to opencode AND export `CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE=builder`.\n2. tmux auto-approve: with `TMUX` set, ARGS must contain `--auto`.\n3. Model enforcement: no `--model` / `--model opus|sonnet|haiku` → exit 1 with the fatal message; provider list must include `opencode`.\n4. Quoting: prompt with spaces must be passed as ONE argument — the Tools copy's `${PROMPT:+\"\\\"\\\"\"}` literal-quote bug must be absent in the canonical version.\n5. Fork identity (opencode): with REAL pointed at a non-fork binary, the wrapper must refuse (exit 1, FATAL message); with the real fork binary, must exec.\n6. Exit-code pass-through: a failing opencode run must return opencode's exit code.\n7. Memory scope: inside tmux with systemd-run present, the exec line must go through systemd-run with MemoryMax; outside tmux, plain exec.\n8. Plugin contract (D1): load the ASES plugin against a fixture `.crosslink/hook-config.json` and verify per-role by_type resolution + the 0-hardcoded-path property (grep already proves it; a load test proves it executes).\n\nRationale: makes D1/D2 reproducible claims instead of size/live-install heuristics, and closes the deploy-path gap the reviewers flagged.\n\n### (b) Alternatives considered\n- **Trust live-install as canonical without tests**: rejected — this is exactly the provenance gap the review flagged.\n- **Reverse-sync only the diff (merge live + Tools changes)**: rejected as ambiguous — the live copy already contains the Tools delta, so \"replace with live\" is simpler and provable; a diff-merge would re-introduce the quoting bug risk.\n\n### (c) What it changes in the 6-step plan\n- Step 1 becomes \"replace Tools copies with live wrappers → run contract battery → commit\" (with the uncommitted delta resolved by the live copy already containing it).\n- Step 2 records functional-superset provenance + a plugin load test.\n- Step 4's TOOLING.md update fixes §1.1/§1.2 false-identical claims and documents the `~/.local/bin` deploy leg.\n- Step 3's wrapper leg deploys to `~/.local/bin`.\n\n### (d) Cheapest discriminating test\nRun the 8-item contract battery against the LIVE wrappers in a scratch PATH before committing anything. If any item fails on the live copy, the canonicalization premise fails — stop and fix the live copy first. Cost: ~10 minutes, no file writes outside scratch.\n\n---\n\n## UPDATED FULL IMPLEMENTATION PLAN (revised ordering)\n\n**Step 0 — Preconditions (NEW; resolves B5+B6 preconditions, Tools uncommitted state)**\n- Commit Tools' uncommitted `scripts/claude` + `.crosslink/rules/global.md` (or stash with a named ref) so Tools worktree is clean.\n- Record provenance snapshot (live wrapper bytes/hashes, plugin versions/sizes, fork binary identity) in the implementation issue.\n- Run the B6 contract battery against live wrappers + ASES plugins (scratch only). Gate: battery passes.\n\n**Step 1 — Wrapper canonicalization (D2; revised by B6)**\n- Replace `Tools/scripts/claude` with live `~/.local/bin/claude`; replace `Tools/scripts/opencode` with live `~/.local/bin/opencode` (crosslink-moe already identical).\n- Re-run contract battery on the Tools copies. Commit on Tools repo (gated).\n\n**Step 2 — Guard-plugin canonicalization (D1; revised by B6)**\n- Copy ASES `.opencode/plugins/{crosslink-guard,orchestrator-guard,rtk-guard}.ts` → `Tools/plugins/`.\n- Record functional-superset + repo-agnostic provenance (not size). Plugin load test against fixture hook-config. Commit on Tools repo.\n\n**Step 3 — sync-tooling.sh (D4; revised by B1/B2/B3/B5)**\n- Manifest: plugins (Tools/plugins → layer/.opencode/plugins + tripn/.opencode/plugins), wrappers (Tools/scripts → ~/.local/bin deploy leg), 2 crosslink skills (Tools/skills → layer/.claude/skills). `rules/` EXCLUDED (B1). tripn leg targets live dirs, NOT `.ases/` (B2).\n- Transaction protocol: dry-run, clean-worktree precondition, local-edit preservation, atomic staging, transaction log, rollback, per-repo verification (B5).\n- Writes `.canonical-manifest.json` (sha256 per file) at each destination; ships `--check` (B3).\n- Tolerance for absent targets: skip EDASES/Execution (don't exist) with a warning; fail only if a declared target repo dir is absent unexpectedly.\n\n**Step 4 — TOOLING.md + knowledge page (D3/D5/D6/D7; non-blocking folds)**\n- Source-of-truth map: own/mirror split + the three-class rules ownership matrix (B1).\n- STALE marker on tripn-astro bundle pointing to tripn repo (D5).\n- §16 fork section: call it a fork, external upstream, canonical embedded-resource source; add binary pin + hook behavior delta (B4).\n- Fix §1.1/§1.2 false-identical claims (B6); document `~/.local/bin` deploy leg.\n- hook-config.json listed as layer-owned with residual-drift note (non-blocking fold).\n- Refresh `tooling` knowledge page (frontmatter says updated 2026-07-31; TOOLING.md Last-audited 2026-07-09 — both go stale post-migration).\n\n**Step 5 — Remove embedded snapshots (D3; revised by B4) — re-sequenced AFTER step 3**\n- Pinned sequence: record binary pin → document behavior delta → `rm -rf Tools/.claude/{hooks,commands,mcp}` → `crosslink init` → verify 6 hooks + new `!= 2` logic → mirror the same pinned sequence in ASES. Alternative: defer until binary rebuild if zero behavior change is required.\n\n**Step 6 — Consumer wiring + enforcement (D1/D2/D4; revised by B3)**\n- Add the guard-plugin startup marker check to crosslink-guard.ts: warn-mode first, hard-fail after sync proven (B3).\n- Add `sync-tooling.sh --check` to the preflight rule.\n- Create implementation issues on the Tools repo crosslink tracker, each referencing #354/D1–D7 (non-blocking fold).\n- ASES keeps its own copy until sync lands (D1) — now with the drift check making \"stale\" visible instead of silent.\n\n---\n\n## RISK REGISTER\n\n| # | Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|---|------|-----------|--------|------------|\n| R1 | Hook behavior change on re-init (returncode semantics) wedges sessions | Med | High | B4 pinned sequence + scratch-write test; defer option documented |\n| R2 | Wrong authoritative plugin copy canonicalized | Low (functional superset proven) | High | B6 provenance + plugin load test; diff evidence recorded, not size |\n| R3 | Sync clobbers layer rules overrides | High if rules synced | High | B1: rules excluded by default; local-edit preservation (B5) |\n| R4 | Wrapper regression after canonicalization (quoting/agent) | Med | Med | B6 contract battery before/after; deploy leg keeps ~/.local/bin in sync |\n| R5 | Crosslink binary staleness invalidates embedded-resource claims | Med | Med | B4 binary pin recorded in TOOLING.md; md5 baseline check (B1 test) |\n| R6 | Tools uncommitted changes lost during cutover | Med | Med | Step 0 commit/stash; B5 clean-worktree precondition |\n| R7 | tripn plugins drift if tripn leg deferred | Med | Med | B2 direct-path sync; fallback: defer tripn leg explicitly + document |\n| R8 | Enforcement check wedges consumers if hard-fail too early | Med | Med | B3 warn-mode transition; hard-fail only after sync proven |\n| R9 | Absent layer targets (EDASES/Execution) break script | Low (known absent) | Low | B2 tolerance: skip + warn |\n| R10 | hook-config.json divergence persists (half the enforcement surface) | High | Med | Non-blocking fold: listed as layer-owned; residual drift documented |\n\n---\n\n## WHAT-NOT-TESTED\n- **sync-tooling.sh not built or executed** — the transaction protocol (B5), marker behavior (B3), and tripn leg (B2) are designed from the verified file reality, not run. The md5 matrix, dir existence, wrapper bytes, plugin refs, hook logic, and git state were all verified directly.\n- **Plugin load against tripn's hook-config.json not executed** — the ASES-superset + repo-agnostic claims are proven by grep/ref-count + source reading, not by running the plugin under tripn's stricter config (comment_discipline=required, signing_enforcement=enforced, orchestrator gates `git worktree remove`).\n- **`crosslink init` not run anywhere** — the NEW hook behavior (returncode != 2 + find_crosslink_binary) is verified by reading fork resources + the installed binary version string, not by executing init in a scratch repo.\n- **No live wrapper executed** — contract battery items are specified, not run; live wrapper bytes are read/diffed, not invoked (read-only task).\n- **B1 md5 matrix covers fork-resources/Tools/ASES/tripn rule files present at time of check; rtk-guard byte-diff across all three repos not re-run** (sizes identical 13893B; content assumed from #358/#359 + ASES/tripn reads).\n- **Cost/time estimates are planning estimates, not benchmarked.**","created_at":"2026-08-14T20:17:37.996912892Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:NTm9QsLsdb/zOTM8xXtaWMU7wteL3FirFVWnTgSAAk0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgttxanJFV/dDT4qsuEY7JxGarkERZbF0WJblKg1FrdYwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA3OyZ8xlf/KB2OrVHZI/4fIDiC6WR4u6Y0QpKW+lx27mD9evqVXdfTuSsvH7Oyna/TNWnyOQcRKKUpWqDuT7nDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:NTm9QsLsdb/zOTM8xXtaWMU7wteL3FirFVWnTgSAAk0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgttxanJFV/dDT4qsuEY7JxGarkERZbF0WJblKg1FrdYwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQELvesd0t/AmTY1KWgDfrRUV8hzpDEdli1cHOoYz4VbqT8YNmU/vJVP/CBSuU8QMnnU/1uKKK5bF3gn4UalE4ws="}
